{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And it shall pass along to Tzennah and its goings out.</b> It is written והיה but read as והיו (plural)." "<b>South of Kadesh Barnea.</b> There are two Kadesh Barneas: the one in the land of Canaan, which is the one mentioned in the book of Joshua among the towns in the land of Canaan; and Kadesh Barnea from where the spies were sent, as it is written in the portion of Matot: 'I sent them from Kadesh Barnea.' And one cannot say they were sent from the Kadesh Barnea in the land of Canaan, for it is established that Moses our teacher did not enter the land. And Kadesh alone is at the edge of the border of the land of Edom." "<b>And it shall go out to Hatzer Addar.</b> Here it implies that it is the district of Addar. And in Joshua it is written similarly: 'and it shall go out to Hatzerah and pass along to Addarah' (וגו׳)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The comment identifies a ketiv-qere difference: the consonantal text has singular והיה while the received reading treats it as plural והיו.", 1 "The final sentence about 'Kadesh alone' appears to refer to a different locale, sometimes identified with Kadesh in the wilderness of Paran, distinct from Kadesh Barnea proper."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:42.537238658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}